Subject: fix(github): address the configured forge in the github subcommands

`fullsend github setup` and `fullsend github set` build their API client with
a bare `gh.New(token)`, which addresses api.github.com by name. On
a GitHub Enterprise Server install, or against any other forge, every one of
these commands leaves the appliance and is refused with credentials that were
never meant for the host they reached — observed as `401 Bad credentials` from
the public API while pointed at a private one.

Every other command in the package already builds its client through
newGitHubLiveClient, which honours the manifest's forge.github.url and falls
back to GITHUB_API_URL. These two now do the same; the status, uninstall
and sync-scaffold commands this patch covered when it was written have since
moved to foreign.go, which already uses newGitHubLiveClient. The fix is the same one
0005 applied to the agents-repo lookup and the status-comment client; this is
the rest of the call sites.

Behaviour on github.com is unchanged: with no manifest URL and no
GITHUB_API_URL the client keeps its default endpoint.

The `gh` import alias is dropped from github.go because these were its only
uses in that file.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh rather than the mirror list. Written to
be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before submitting it as a
human-authored change.

